# Thalyx owns the boot.
#
# This file is the whole of the claim in `Decision-Capa-vs-SO-Nuevo.md`, made
# concrete. What an Alpine base would put here is:
#
#     tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty1
#
# which is a login, which is a shell, which makes Thalyx a program you run
# after identifying yourself to somebody else's system. Nobody ever decreed
# that login. It is what the base hands you for free if this file is left
# alone, and leaving it alone would satisfy the decree on paper while breaking
# it in the artefact.
#
# There is no getty here and no shell in the image. That is not a restriction
# with a workaround behind it — there is nothing behind it.

::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default

# The machine's session. If it dies, it comes back; there is nothing else for
# the machine to be doing.
tty1::respawn:/usr/bin/thalyx session

# Consoles 2-4 get the same thing rather than a getty, so that switching away
# does not quietly land somebody in a shell that was not supposed to exist.
tty2::respawn:/usr/bin/thalyx session
tty3::respawn:/usr/bin/thalyx session

::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
